Alembic migrations for the crude-oil paper-trading backend.

The database URL is read from conf/*.yaml (database.url, which honours the
DATABASE_URL env var), not from alembic.ini, so these migrations always target
the same database the application uses.

Every migration must run clean on both SQLite and MySQL. env.py enables
render_as_batch on SQLite so ALTERs are emitted as table rebuilds.

  alembic upgrade head        # apply
  alembic downgrade -1        # roll back one
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."
